* The rename is complete. The product file has `sdh_resv` and no `sectorsize`. Its only readers are the SDH readback and that arm's debug line. The struct is zeroed at init (`dev_wdc.c:2083-2084`). READ.
* Decode is bit 6, drive is bit 4, head is `idata & 0xf`, and bits 7 and 5 are `idata & 0xa0`. READ.
* Readback is byte-exact for every select byte. Those four fields partition bits 7 and 5, bit 6, bit 4, and bits 3�?"0, and the readback ORs them back together. DERIVED. `0x00`, `0x40`, `0x4c`, `0xa0`, `0xb3`, `0xe0`, `0xe5`, and `0xff` all round-trip.
* Both arms are `512 * (int64_t)(((d->head & 0xf) << 24) + (cyl << 8) + d->sector)`. On the write side that assignment sits above `write_in_progress`, `write_count`, and `write_offset` (`:569-571`). Both `printf`s are gone. READ.
* The cast widens the multiply, which is the overflow. The sum is still done in `int`. For every LBA28 taskfile byte it fits: the maximum is `0x0FFFFFFF` (268435455), below 2A3A1�^'1. `512 * LBA` is what overflows a 32-bit `int`. V15, the unwidened product, served sector 5 on `lba h1` (`0xfffa0005` in `raw_mut/V15.out`). DERIVED; that log line is READ. The comment's "any head != 0" is the case the table measured. A head-0 LBA at or above 2A�A� overflows a 32-bit product as well, and this cast covers that range too.
* `cyl = cyl_hi * 256 + cyl_lo` (`:467`, `:558`), so `(cyl << 8) + sector + (head_nibble << 24)` is LBA28, with the sector register not decremented. Tag checks: 70 �+' `0xffb90046`, 69 �+' `0xffba0045`, 256 �+' `0xfeff0100`, 1007 �+' `0xfc1003ef`, 0 �+' `0xffff0000`. DERIVED. The witness files show those values. READ.
* Word 49's two bytes are still 0. Words 60�?"61 are filled from `total_size / 512` (`:441-445`). The capacity sentence is true. READ.
* `d->lba` has one writer (`:2019`) and two address readers (`:475`, `:565`). READ. The CHS formula and its casts are unchanged around the new arms. READ. A whole-file `git diff HEAD` was not re-run here, so "no other hunk in this file" past those anchors is NOT CHECKABLE.
* Geometry 16/63 with cylinders rounded up is `diskimage.c:270-271` and `:295-297`. 4096 sectors �+' 5 cylinders �+' 5040. DERIVED from that code. READ.
* The `est/` twin is NOT CHECKABLE. This tree has no `est/`. `dev_wdc.c` is not on the SEC-only list in `tools/est_divergence.txt`, so check A requires the same five hunks in the twin.

